BEST Strategy Template (v4) — signal-source template, by design produces zero trades

By-design exclusion: entry conditions are `bull = (ext_source == 1)` and
`bear = (ext_source == -1)`, where `ext_source` defaults to `close`.
`close` is never exactly ±1 on any real price feed, so no entries ever trigger.
This is not a runner defect — the strategy is a template requiring the caller to
supply an external signal series as `ext_source`.

Excluded from the 10/10 TV-match denominator: zero-entry-by-design strategies
are not falsifiable against TradingView Strategy Tester output.

To reactivate: replace the `ext_source` default with a real signal indicator
(e.g. an RSI crossover) that produces values of exactly +1 or -1 before removing
this skip sidecar.
